WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.878
A correlated subquery uses a value from the current
outer row For

00:00:05.891 --> 00:00:11.403
example the outer query may define patients as p
Inside

00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:18.023
the subquery a condition may compare a child patient
ID with p patient ID When

00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:24.155
the outer patient changes the inner query's matching
value changes too This

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:27.919
is why correlated subqueries are useful for per-row
calculations
